{"availability":"available","full":"jasper-note/jasper","name":"jasper","description":"Lightweight read-write Joplin-compatible client — local Rust server + browser SPA. Live in-browser WASM demo.","category":"Productivity","language":"Rust","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-29T11:17:48Z","updated":"2026-10-02T09:42:05Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://jasper-note.github.io/jasper/","topics":["axum","joplin","markdown","note-taking","rust","self-hosted","svelte","wasm","webassembly","webdav"],"demo":"https://jasper-note.github.io/jasper/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:03.945Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:03.945Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:03.945Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T00:00:03.945Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Svelte","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🌐 Live demo (runs entirely in your browser via WASM, no server):","A lightweight, read-write Joplin-compatible client: a local Rust (axum) server + browser SPA — no Electron, Tauri, or WebView. It reads and writes your existing Joplin sync library directly, so edits are picked up by Joplin on its next sync.","Not affiliated with Joplin. Jasper is an independent, unofficial project that is merely compatible with the open Joplin sync format. It is not produced, sponsored, endorsed by, or otherwise legally affiliated with Joplin or its authors. \"Joplin\" is a trademark of its respective owner and is used here only nominatively, to describe data-format compatibility."],"features":["Tiny & fast — the Rust backend stays resident at 10 MB and starts almost instantly. No 200 MB Electron runtime.","Cross-platform — a single binary on macOS / Windows / Linux; the UI is just a browser tab.","Your data, your files — operates directly on the Joplin sync format (.md items + .resource/ blobs). Nothing is locked into a new database.","Data sources: local folder or WebDAV (Nextcloud, etc.).","Three-pane UI: notebook tree (nested, with note counts) · note list · reader/editor."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7236470c9c2c2914b109f4d2b7dbc34053891bd637a9759b89a5a4ab062f5e93","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:04.063Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:04.063Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"🌐 Live demo (runs entirely in your browser via WASM, no server):","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"Optional access password (Settings → Access control): once set, every write requires login; visitors without a session get read-only access or nothing, per the rule below.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Passwordless read toggle: on lets logged-out visitors browse read-only (scoped by a per-notebook allow/deny list); off shows a login gate to anyone without a session — handy for sharing an instance for others to read.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"7236470c9c2c2914b109f4d2b7dbc34053891bd637a9759b89a5a4ab062f5e93","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:04.064Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T09:42:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jasper-note/jasper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T00:00:04.067Z","hash":"7236470c9c2c2914b109f4d2b7dbc34053891bd637a9759b89a5a4ab062f5e93","originalBytes":7358,"storedBytes":7358,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["joplin","note","only","sync","access","api","editor","local","browser","docs","jasper","library","markdown","notes","open","resource","resources","screenshots","search","server","webdav","control","data","live","one","run","rust","source","axum","build","cache","codemirror","config","demo","